      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0056","sequence":68,
      "meaning":"Having understood Raghubīra’s majesty, Satī is afraid and conceals the truth from Śiva: she says she made no test, merely bowed as he had, and now fully trusts his words. Entering meditation, Śaṅkara sees everything she did. He bows to Rāma’s māyā, which impelled Satī to speak falsely, and reflects that Hari’s will and destiny are powerful. Because Satī assumed Sītā’s form, Śiva feels profound grief: if he now loves her as wife, the path of devotion would be erased and wrong would result. Yet he cannot abandon one so pure, while marital love would be a grave sin. Maheśa says nothing openly, though anguish deepens in his heart.",
