      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0057","sequence":69,
      "meaning":"Śaṅkara bows to the Lord’s feet, remembers Rāma, and resolves inwardly that he will not meet Satī as wife while she bears this body. Keeping Raghubīra in mind, the steadfast Śiva journeys home. A beautiful heavenly voice praises Maheśa’s firm devotion and declares that no one but this mighty divine devotee of Rāma could make such a vow. Alarmed, Satī asks the compassionate Lord what vow he made, but Tripura’s foe does not tell her despite repeated questions. She infers that the all-knowing Śiva knows her deception and laments her naturally dull ignorance. Love’s beautiful way is like milk sold blended with water: when the acid of deceit enters, the flavor separates and is lost.",
