    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0058","sequence":70,
      "meaning":"Reflecting on her deed, Satī bears indescribable anxiety. She recognizes that unfathomably compassionate Śiva does not expose her offense; seeing his changed manner, she is distraught that he has abandoned her. Conscious of her sin, she cannot speak and her heart burns like a potter’s kiln. Knowing her sorrow, Vṛṣaketu tells pleasing stories along the road until Viśvanātha reaches Kailāsa. Remembering his vow, Śambhu sits in lotus posture beneath the banyan, recollects his essential nature, and enters boundless, unbroken samādhi. Satī dwells at Kailāsa in deep distress; no one knows the secret, and each day passes like an age.",
