    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0059","sequence":71,
      "meaning":"Ever-new sorrow weighs on Satī: when will she cross this ocean of pain? She dishonored Raghupati and deemed her husband’s words false; the Creator has given the fitting fruit of her act. She asks fate why it keeps her alive while Śaṅkara is turned away. Unable to express her remorse, the wise Satī remembers Rāma inwardly. If the Lord truly is merciful to the lowly and the Vedas praise him as remover of affliction, she prays with joined palms that this body may quickly fall away. If her love for Śiva’s feet and her vow in thought, act and word are true, she asks the all-seeing Lord swiftly to devise a painless death that ends her unbearable calamity.",
