    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0060","sequence":72,
      "meaning":"Thus Prajāpati’s daughter endures terrible, indescribable grief. After eighty-seven thousand years, imperishable Śambhu leaves samādhi and begins remembering Rāma’s name. Satī realizes that the Lord of the world is awake, bows at his feet, and Śaṅkara gives her a seat before him. He begins telling the nectar-sweet story of Hari. At that time Dakṣa becomes Prajāpati: Brahmā judges him qualified and appoints him leader of the progenitors. Great authority fills Dakṣa’s heart with pride—for no one is born who gains dominion without intoxication. Dakṣa summons all the sages and begins a great sacrifice, respectfully inviting every god entitled to a sacrificial share.",
